# A hosted child's place with a plain answer bound to a name, whose constant field reads a
# building `if`'s late plain result written below it (Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and
# cycles": any line may use any name the block binds, and the order of a group's lines
# decides positions and nothing else; ch. 9: a supplier answers a hosted place, its plain
# answer the place's first value, asked by the element as built). Nothing here is a cycle:
# the `if` reads nothing of the place. The same place of the World's lowers
# (conformance/sem-ch04-late-value-above-in-dynamic-place-field and its kin). Reaches
# `BindLate`'s marker "the late result `k` read at its block's build" on prismc-fd1.
# Written by Claude (sweep-7, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.* | Pad.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

tag Pad.Ask of Element Text:
    name: Text

@Inner: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Inner loud:
    a <- Pad.Ask(name="ask {k}")                                       # [0]
    Ui.Label($text=$"asked {a}")                                       # [1]
    k <- if loud:
        Ui.Label($text=$"loud")                                        # [2]
        @ "x"
    else:
        @ "y"

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    ignore <- @Host (@Inner loud), \|p, e| match e:           # 0/[p]
        Pad.Ask(name=n): @ "yes {n}"
        otherwise: @Element e
